    "result_text": "The full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`) passes and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the age-band feature on `POST /api/owners` (returned via `GET /api/owners/{id}`) so a request may include `birthDate` (ISO), and the owner's derived `ageBand` is returned as `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364) or `SENIOR` (65+), computed against the registration date.\n\nChanges, each placed where the responsibility belongs:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the optional `birthDate` input to the `OwnerFields` schema and the read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs and MapStruct mappings are generated from this, so no hand-written DTO/mapper edits were needed.\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (hsqldb is what the tests use, since its profile runs with `ddl-auto=none` from `schema.sql`).\n- **`model/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 a small enum that owns the age-to-band classification: `AgeBand.on(birthDate, referenceDate)` computes completed-years age via `Period.between` and maps it to the band, returning `null` when either date is absent. This mirrors the existing `CustomerCode`/`RegistrationDatePolicy` idiom rather than inlining the logic.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field with accessors and a derived `getAgeBand()` that delegates to `AgeBand.on(birthDate, registrationDate)`. Because `registrationDate` is resolved (defaulted/rolled to a business day) at `@PrePersist`, the band is always computed against the effective registration date, consistent with the other registration-date-derived getters.\n\nMapStruct auto-generated the `AgeBand \u2192 OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum` conversion and the `birthDate` field mappings. The acceptance test (`coreDerivesAgeBand`: birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) and the full suite pass.",
